axton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spaxton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spaxton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spaxton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spaxton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spaxton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spaxton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T00:59:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T00:59:25Z","body":"This is fairly easily testable through gaming controllers - hooking up an XBox controller and plugging in a microphone to its 9mm jack allows Godot to receive microphone input, and it has more than 2 channels.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955710052/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4449088302","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-4449088302","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":4449088302,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCS-zLg","user":{"login":"HenryHa993","id":61506778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNTA2Nzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61506778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993","html_url":"https://github.com/HenryHa993","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HenryHa993/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T08:39:54Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T08:39:54Z","body":"Any updates on getting this through?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4449088302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5217864733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5217864733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5217864733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNwJMHQ","user":{"login":"SleeeepyZhou","id":80639626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjM5NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80639626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou","html_url":"https://github.com/SleeeepyZhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T13:47:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T13:47:13Z","body":"> None of the audio backends implemented in Godot seem to support more than 2 channel input audio devices. Some seem to handle it silently (like CoreAudio), others print a warning (like PulseAudio).\r\n> \r\n> I'd argue that for consistency sake, either all backends should be extended, or only the fist two channels should be used in all. But generally silently mixing input channels together under the hood is likely not a good idea. If other channels of an input device serve other purpose than traditional microphone input, e.g. if they represent noise cancellation microphones - when mixed with the intended first two channels, may produce unexpected results.\r\n> \r\n> If there's no consensus on the above mentioned, the code looks fine, technically addresses the issue, just minor errors as I pointed out in the review comments. However, I was unable to test and verify the fix on my setup.\r\n> \r\n> Worth pointing out, the original issue was \"Godot does not listen to microphones with over 2 channels\", while the PR adds new behavior of \"downmixing all the extra input channels to 2\" and technically Godot still doesn't provide more than 2 channels of input audio to the user after this PR.\r\n\r\nThat's the issue, but according to the information I've found, there seems to be no suitable way to distinguish what multiple microphone inputs are. (For example🤔, my laptop actually has five microphone inputs, three of which are used for noise reduction, and it seems that their IDs are not simply confirmed as the first two. So I can't directly identify the two main inputs and discard the others.🤪)\r\n\r\nThen, it has been a year since this PR was submitted, and I'm not sure why it hasn't been merged yet.🤔","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5217864733/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5218407456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5218407456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5218407456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNwqUIA","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T14:37:00Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T14:37:00Z","body":"\r\n> That's the issue, but according to the information I've found, there seems to be no suitable way to distinguish what multiple microphone inputs are. (For example🤔, my laptop actually has five microphone inputs, three of which are used for noise reduction, and it seems that their IDs are not simply confirmed as the first two. So I can't directly identify the two main inputs and discard the others.🤪)\r\n\r\nYeah, that's a real problem. But doesn't have to be on Godot to handle all of this. Usually there's a way to set up just 1-2 channel input device in the OS audio settings, or in the driver app. E.g. if some mics are used for noise cancellation, this process runs somewhere, outputting to a useable \"virtual\" audio input device, which is what meant to be used by other applications.\r\n\r\nIt is most common that apps use only the first two channels, or use whatever driver gives them. And it's up to the user to ensure the app receives the correct device. As for the game audio engines, it's common provide API to select the device, which would just make it so the user doesn't have to go to OS audio settings and set the \"microphone\" used by the game.\r\nBut doing some hidden mixing might be not expected by the user. Especially if they compare mic check form some app vs mic input in Godot.\r\n\r\n🤷‍♂️ ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5218407456/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5218677637","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5218677637","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5218677637,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNw6zhQ","user":{"login":"SleeeepyZhou","id":80639626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjM5NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80639626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou","html_url":"https://github.com/SleeeepyZhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T15:03:16Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T15:03:16Z","body":"> > That's the issue, but according to the information I've found, there seems to be no suitable way to distinguish what multiple microphone inputs are. (For example🤔, my laptop actually has five microphone inputs, three of which are used for noise reduction, and it seems that their IDs are not simply confirmed as the first two. So I can't directly identify the two main inputs and discard the others.🤪)\r\n> \r\n> Yeah, that's a real problem. But doesn't have to be on Godot to handle all of this. Usually there's a way to set up just 1-2 channel input device in the OS audio settings, or in the driver app. E.g. if some mics are used for noise cancellation, this process runs somewhere, outputting to a useable \"virtual\" audio input device, which is what meant to be used by other applications.\r\n> \r\n> It is most common that apps use only the first two channels, or use whatever driver gives them. And it's up to the user to ensure the app receives the correct device. As for the game audio engines, it's common provide API to select the device, which would just make it so the user doesn't have to go to OS audio settings and set the \"microphone\" used by the game. But doing some hidden mixing might be not expected by the user. Especially if they compare mic check form some app vs mic input in Godot.\r\n> \r\n> 🤷‍♂️\r\n\r\nYeah, the cross‑backend consistency thing is definitely a valid concern. 👀\r\nRealistically though, this PR is just trying to fix the WASAPI‑specific headache where multi‑channel mics straight‑up refuse to open on Windows. Getting all the other backends in sync can be future work — each of them needs actual hardware to test anyway.\r\nThat OS‑level virtual device workaround works great if it’s available, but a lot of end‑users won’t know or bother digging into Windows sound settings. Before this PR, these multi‑channel mics are just completely dead in Godot, no fallback at all.\r\n\r\n🐱","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5218677637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5219257218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5219257218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5219257218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNxeLgg","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T15:59:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T15:59:42Z","body":"> That OS‑level virtual device workaround works great if it’s available, but a lot of end‑users won’t know or bother digging into Windows sound settings.\r\n\r\nThat's why usually games expose mic audio input device in audio settings. When it matters, you should be able to chose what you know is the proper mic.\r\n\r\nI see three choices here:\r\n1. Mix down all the channels to two, i.e. keep PR as is (assuming you fix the minor details I commented about in the review 👀).\r\n2. Only read from the first two channels (like every other audio backend implemented in Godot).\r\n3. Make this a config/API to either read from the first two channels, discarding the rest, or downmix.\r\n\r\nIn either case more-than-2-channel audio input devices will be functional.\r\n\r\nI'm personally leaning towards the option 2, as it's consistent with the other backends. But I'm not the one who's going to be merging this. Maybe this can be brought up on audio dev meeting.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5219257218/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5219357536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5219357536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5219357536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNxkTYA","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:08:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T16:09:59Z","body":"I agree with the sentiment expressed by Jaytheway: Combining microphone channels is not appropriate behaviour for Godot when there are more than 2 channels because it is impossible to know what these input channels may be used for or how the user may want them to be handled.\r\n\r\n> Realistically though, this PR is just trying to fix the WASAPI‑specific headache where multi‑channel mics straight‑up refuse to open on Windows.\r\n\r\nI believe the only reasonable ways to address this existing issue are:\r\n1. keep the first two channels and discard later channels (edit: [option 2 from Joytheway's comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5219257218))\r\n2. introduce support for > 2 channel input all on platforms throughout Godot as a first-class feature","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5219357536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5220516894","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5220516894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5220516894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNyrEHg","user":{"login":"SleeeepyZhou","id":80639626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjM5NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80639626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou","html_url":"https://github.com/SleeeepyZhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T18:11:08Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T18:11:08Z","body":">  Only read from the first two channels (like every other audio backend implemented in Godot).\r\n\r\nGot it, thanks for laying out these options. 🥳\r\n\r\n> I believe the only reasonable ways to address this existing issue are:\r\n> \r\n> 1. keep the first two channels and discard later channels (edit: [option 2 from Joytheway's comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5219257218))\r\n> 2. introduce support for > 2 channel input all on platforms throughout Godot as a first-class feature\r\n\r\nI'm fine moving forward with option 2: read only the first two channels and discard the rest.\r\nThis resolves the main blocker — multi‑channel microphones will no longer fail to open on Windows, while keeping WASAPI aligned with other Godot audio backends.\r\n﻿\r\nIt’s not ideal for niche hardware where usable audio isn’t on channel 0/1, but those edge‑cases can be revisited later if we ever add a config/API for this.\r\n﻿\r\nI will adjust the code logic and fix those minor review issues in my next commit.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5220516894/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5227522287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5227522287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5227522287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN5Wo7w","user":{"login":"SleeeepyZhou","id":80639626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjM5NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80639626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou","html_url":"https://github.com/SleeeepyZhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-08T18:32:17Z","updated_at":"2026-08-08T18:32:17Z","body":"> There are still two issues pointed out in comments to resolve.\r\n> \r\n> Edit: never mind, I just reread:\r\n> \r\n> > I will adjust the code logic and fix those minor review issues in my next commit.\r\n> \r\n> ..if going with option to only keep the first 2 channels, this block is irrelevant\r\n\r\nGot it~🥳","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5227522287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5230299342","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5230299342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5230299342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN8AIzg","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T07:09:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T07:11:59Z","body":"I'm not sure if GitHub is showing the right changes for the review, it still shows the old `>2` channels branch present.\r\nWhereas the entire thing should be just this:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (flags & AUDCLNT_BUFFERFLAGS_SILENT) {\r\n\tl = r = 0;\r\n} else {\r\n\tif (ad->audio_input.channels >= 2) {\r\n\t\tl = read_sample(ad->audio_input.format_tag, ad->audio_input.bits_per_sample, data, j * ad->audio_input.channels);\r\n\t\tr = read_sample(ad->audio_input.format_tag, ad->audio_input.bits_per_sample, data, j * ad->audio_input.channels + 1);\r\n\t} else if (ad->audio_input.channels == 1) {\r\n\t\tl = r = read_sample(ad->audio_input.format_tag, ad->audio_input.bits_per_sample, data, j);\r\n\t} else {\r\n\t\tl = r = 0;\r\n\t\tERR_PRINT(\"WASAPI: unsupported channel count in microphone!\");\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5230299342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5241699850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5241699850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5241699850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOG3-Cg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T14:33:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T14:33:02Z","body":"No need to squash this until it's been approved by a maintainer","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5241699850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5276200299","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5276200299","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5276200299,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOnxtaw","user":{"login":"LukePH","id":2411696,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MTE2OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2411696?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH","html_url":"https://github.com/LukePH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LukePH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T05:06:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T05:12:22Z","body":"I think this PR should be merged with a high priority even if it needs some follow up later. Laptops with 5 channel mic inputs are getting quite common, I happen to have 2 laptops with them and so do some friends.\r\n\r\nJust enabling 'Enable Input' in the project settings on these laptops creates multi gigabyte godot.log after a few minutes in game! From \r\n\"WASAPI: unsupported channel count in microphone!\" spam written to the logs every frame even while mic input is not being used by the game.\r\n\r\nWhich means no one should ship a game with 'Enable Input' on right now. The log spam from this warning makes this way worse then the audio just being broken, games will run out of disk space on these laptops.\r\n\r\nI've tested an engine build with this pull request applied and can confirm that mic audio works great on my laptop (with 5 channels) after applying this fix.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5276200299/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5277482319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5277482319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5277482319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOo_9Tw","user":{"login":"SleeeepyZhou","id":80639626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjM5NjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80639626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou","html_url":"https://github.com/SleeeepyZhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleeeepyZhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T07:40:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T07:40:47Z","body":"> I think this PR should be merged with a high priority even if it needs some follow up later. Laptops with 5 channel mic inputs are getting quite common, I happen to have 2 laptops with them and so do some friends.\r\n> \r\n> Just enabling 'Enable Input' in the project settings on these laptops creates multi gigabyte godot.log after a few minutes in game! From \"WASAPI: unsupported channel count in microphone!\" spam written to the logs every frame even while mic input is not being used by the game.\r\n> \r\n> Which means no one should ship a game with 'Enable Input' on right now. The log spam from this warning makes this way worse then the audio just being broken, games will run out of disk space on these laptops.\r\n> \r\n> I've tested an engine build with this pull request applied and can confirm that mic audio works great on my laptop (with 5 channels) after applying this fix.\r\n\r\nSo glad this fix could help! I also own a 5-channel laptop and ran into exactly the same annoying log spam issue myself. It's really rewarding to resolve this widespread pain point for everyone.🥳🥳😆","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5277482319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5302425001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#issuecomment-5302425001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101673","id":5302425001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPAyVqQ","user":{"login":"SleeeepyZhou","id":80639626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjM5NjI2","avatar_url":"ht